    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe membership-cap mechanism itself is clean and idiomatic: `CapMembershipLevel` follows the established `Assign*` step pattern exactly (`@Val Owner`, `OwnerRepository`, `findAll()` loop, writes a field onto the owner so the mapper derives without a DB round-trip \u2014 matching `AssignHouseholdSize`'s stated rationale), and the `membershipLevel` / `uncappedMembershipLevel` split in `OwnerMapper` is a natural, well-documented decomposition. No concerns there.\n\nThe problem is the bundled, out-of-scope rewrite of `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` and the incoherent state it leaves behind.\n\n1. **Unrelated business-rule change smuggled into a membership-cap feature.** The diff deletes the entire household-duplicate rejection branch (and the `sharesHousehold` bypass read) from `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`. The spec is solely about capping `membershipLevel`; it does not require relaxing duplicate detection. Multiple household members were already creatable via `sharesHousehold=true`, so the cap feature works without touching this guard. Loosening a separate 409 rule under the banner of this feature is not an additive, coherent change \u2014 it belongs in its own change (if intended at all).\n\n2. **Neighboring javadocs now describe behavior that no longer exists.** The removal was made in one class but the surrounding steps still document the old contract, leaving contradictory docs a maintainer can't trust:\n   - `AssignHousehold` (lines 14\u201316): \"The duplicate guard (`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`) already decided whether this owner may be created in its household; `sharesHousehold` only bypasses that guard\" \u2014 `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` no longer does household-based rejection and no longer reads `sharesHousehold`.\n   - `AssignPossibleDuplicate` (lines 18\u201319): \"(A non-declared owner sharing a household is rejected outright by `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`, so it never reaches this step.)\" \u2014 this invariant is now false; such owners now reach this step, which changes how the `sharesHousehold` bypass at line 33 is reached.\n   - `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (around lines 2108, 2203) still describes `sharesHousehold` as allowing creation past the same-household 409 and documents the household-duplicate rejection.\n\n3. **`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`'s own class javadoc** was updated, but the result is that `sharesHousehold` is now a field some steps read (`AssignPossibleDuplicate`) and some no longer do, with the cross-references between the three steps no longer consistent. Either keep the household guard out of this change, or finish the job: update `AssignHousehold`/`AssignPossibleDuplicate` javadocs and the OpenAPI descriptions so the pipeline documents one coherent story.\n\nSuggested resolution: drop the `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` edit from this change (the cap feature stands on its own), or, if the relaxation is genuinely intended, land it with all stale references above corrected in the same change.",
